# GoKey @TAG@ - pre-release

**This build does not type Vietnamese.** The payload is the headless engine CLI inside a
stub .app. This release proves the download, install and licence path; it says nothing
about the input method. MAC-002 replaces the payload.

## macOS will refuse it once. That is expected.

This build is **ad-hoc signed and not notarised**. There is no paid Apple Developer
Program membership behind it, so macOS has no identity to vouch for the build and
Gatekeeper rejects the first launch. Nothing is wrong with the download.

1. Open the dmg and drag **GoKey.app** into **Applications**.
2. In Applications, **right-click (or Control-click) > Open**, then **Open** in the
   dialog. A double-click will not work: the first dialog has no Open button.
3. After that it opens normally.

Or drop the quarantine flag:

    xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/GoKey.app

## Verify the download

    shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS

| file | what it is |
| --- | --- |
| GoKey-@VERSION@-@BUILD@.dmg | ad-hoc signed, universal (arm64 + x86_64) |
| source.tar.gz | corresponding source, `git archive` of @TAG@ |
| SHA256SUMS | checksums for the two files above |
| LICENSE.txt, NOTICE.md | GPL-3.0 licence and upstream attribution |
| SOURCE-OFFER.txt | where the source for this exact build lives |

## Provenance

- tag @TAG@ (@TAG_TYPE@) -> commit @SHA@, an ancestor of main
- main at build time: @MAIN_TIP@
- built with @TOOLCHAIN@ on macos-15
- `spctl` rejects both the dmg and the app; CI asserts that rather than skipping it

